{#
  The signature dialog, shared by every module that signs a document
  (issue #926, lot C1; ARCHITECTURE.md §8.125, design.md §7.5). The page
  renders it once per document to sign, and a button of its own opens it:

      <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary"
              data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#countersign-12">Contresigner</button>
      {% include 'partials/signature_dialog.html.twig' with {
          id: 'countersign-12',
          title: 'Contresigner le contrat',
          action: '/mes-locations/contrat-contresigner',
          fields: { booking_id: 12, document_id: 40 },
          consequence: 'Votre signature est ajoutée sur une dernière page…',
          has_stored_signature: true,
          manage_return: '/mes-locations/chalet/reservations/12',
      } only %}

  **The dialog is the confirmation.** Nothing is signed until « Signer le
  document »; « Annuler » posts nothing. So the form carries no
  data-confirm: a second question after this one would teach the reader
  to dismiss both.

  Three modes:
  - stored (`has_stored_signature`): the ticket's sentence, the module's
    consequence, a small preview of the signature — fetched from
    /account/signature/image by signature-dialog.js when the dialog opens
    (decision Q5), never written into this page, which may be cached —
    and « Gérer ma signature » for whoever wants another one (decision Q3:
    no other drawing for one document);
  - new: the pad, an optional import (`allow_import`, default true) and
    « Mémoriser ma signature dans mon compte pour une utilisation
    future » (`allow_remember`, default true), never rendered checked;
  - witness (`witness: true`, ticket §6a): a person without an account,
    their typed name (`signer_name`, required), drawing only — no import,
    no box, nothing kept.

  Parameters: `id`, `title`, `action`, `consequence` (the module's own
  sentence: what signing does), `fields` (hidden fields, name → value),
  and the mode options above. `manage_return` is where « Gérer ma
  signature » brings the visitor back to. `form_attributes` (name → value)
  adds attributes to the form — a page whose script turns forms into
  fetches passes what makes it stand aside (Locations: `data-async: 'off'`),
  since an open dialog does not survive its panels being re-rendered. The
  page loads signature-pad.js then signature-dialog.js, which wires a
  dialog again when it opens — a re-rendered panel brings a fresh copy.

  Never an account id among the fields: whose signature it is, is the
  session's to say (Core\Signature\SignatureSubmission).
#}
{% set witness = witness|default(false) %}
{% set stored = not witness and has_stored_signature|default(false) %}
{% set allow_import = not witness and (allow_import is defined ? allow_import : true) %}
{% set allow_remember = not witness and (allow_remember is defined ? allow_remember : true) %}
{% set form_id = id ~ '-form' %}
{% embed 'partials/modal.html.twig' with {
    id: id,
    title: title,
    static_backdrop: true,
    form_id: form_id,
    stored: stored,
    witness: witness,
    allow_import: allow_import,
    allow_remember: allow_remember,
    action: action,
    fields: fields|default({}),
    consequence: consequence|default(''),
    manage_return: manage_return|default(''),
    form_attributes: form_attributes|default({}),
} only %}
    {% block body %}
        <form method="post" action="{{ action }}" id="{{ form_id }}" enctype="multipart/form-data"
              data-signature-form data-signature-dialog-form
              data-signature-mode="{{ witness ? 'witness' : (stored ? 'stored' : 'new') }}"
              {%- for name, value in form_attributes %} {{ name|e('html_attr') }}="{{ value }}"{% endfor %}>
            {{ csrf_field()|raw }}
            {% for name, value in fields %}
                <input type="hidden" name="{{ name }}" value="{{ value }}">
            {% endfor %}
            <input type="hidden" name="signature_source" value="{{ stored ? 'stored' : 'new' }}">

            {% if stored %}
                <p>Ce document sera signé avec la signature enregistrée dans votre compte. Vérifiez son contenu avant de confirmer.</p>
                {% if consequence %}<p>{{ consequence }}</p>{% endif %}
                {# Filled by signature-dialog.js when the dialog opens, emptied when it closes. #}
                <div class="border rounded bg-white p-2 mb-2 text-center" data-signature-preview
                     style="min-height: 4rem;"></div>
                <p class="small mb-0">
                    <a href="/account/signature{{ manage_return ? '?retour=' ~ manage_return|url_encode : '' }}">Gérer ma signature</a>
                </p>
            {% else %}
                {% if consequence %}<p>{{ consequence }}</p>{% endif %}
                {% if witness %}
                    <div class="mb-3">
                        <label class="form-label" for="{{ id }}-signer-name">Nom de la personne qui signe</label>
                        <input type="text" class="form-control" id="{{ id }}-signer-name" name="signer_name"
                               maxlength="120" required autocomplete="off">
                    </div>
                {% endif %}
                <input type="hidden" name="signature_data" value="">

                <p class="form-label mb-1" id="{{ id }}-pad-label">{{ witness ? 'Signature' : 'Tracez votre signature' }}</p>
                {#
                  Traced with a pointer, so no role of its own: « img »
                  would tell assistive technology there is nothing to do
                  here. Without a pointer, the import below is the way in.
                #}
                <canvas data-signature-pad width="900" height="300"
                        aria-labelledby="{{ id }}-pad-label"
                        class="border rounded bg-white w-100 d-block" style="aspect-ratio: 3 / 1;"></canvas>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary mt-2" data-signature-clear>Effacer</button>

                {% if allow_import %}
                    <div class="mt-3">
                        <label class="form-label" for="{{ id }}-file">Ou importez une image de votre signature</label>
                        <input type="file" class="form-control" id="{{ id }}-file" name="signature_file"
                               accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp" aria-describedby="{{ id }}-file-help">
                        <p class="form-text" id="{{ id }}-file-help">PNG, JPEG ou WebP, 5 Mo au plus.</p>
                    </div>
                {% endif %}

                {% if allow_remember %}
                    <div class="form-check mt-3">
                        <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="remember_signature" value="1"
                               id="{{ id }}-remember" aria-describedby="{{ id }}-remember-help">
                        <label class="form-check-label" for="{{ id }}-remember">Mémoriser ma signature dans mon compte pour une utilisation future</label>
                        <p class="form-text mb-0" id="{{ id }}-remember-help">
                            Sans cette case, la signature sert à ce document seulement et n'est pas gardée.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                {% endif %}

                <p class="text-danger small mt-2 mb-0" data-signature-missing hidden role="alert">
                    {{ allow_import ? "Tracez votre signature ou importez-en l'image." : 'Tracez la signature dans le cadre.' }}
                </p>
            {% endif %}
        </form>
    {% endblock %}
    {% block footer %}
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Annuler</button>
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" form="{{ form_id }}">Signer le document</button>
    {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
